The Cushion Swap File is Daniel Ramos's design, his "Dynamic Swap Parachute"
(2026-08-01): the decision rules, thresholds and arithmetic of
usr/sbin/cushion-swap and the test harness tests/test_swap_parachute.sh are
his. The wake-up helper uses the kernel's pressure stall information (PSI),
by Johannes Weiner, with the trigger interface by Suren Baghdasaryan
(Linux kernel/sched/psi.c). No code from swapspace or systemd-oomd is
included; README.md compares them.

